                    "a": "The rights of children are still not fully protected despite CRC and UDHR, because the enforcement of human rights is weak — fundamental rights can be enforced through the court, while respect for human rights is the responsibility of states. UDHR 1948 was made to protect the rights of adults (above 18 years), so a separate convention was needed for children. Despite the law, poverty, child labour and bonded labour continue and implementation is weak.",
