                    "q": "VII. We may feel internal injury or altitude sickness at higher or lower altitudes than sea level because: a. The pressure of our body remains the same b. Our body adjusts the pressure slowly c. Our body adjust the pressure quickly d. Our body unable to adjust the pressure",
                    "a": "(b) Our body adjusts the pressure slowly — the body needs time to equalize with the changing atmospheric pressure, and while it adjusts, the difference in pressure is felt (for example, the ears pop in an airplane as they try to match the pressure)."
