              {
                "label": "8",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "q": "Q8. State Pascal's Law and explain an application of this law.",
                    "a": "Pascal's law (Pascal's Principle) states that pressure applied to an enclosed liquid is transmitted equally to every part of the liquid. Application — Hydraulic Jack: a hydraulic jack is a device used to lift heavy loads. It is light, compact and portable, but capable of exerting great force. The device pushes liquid against a piston, pressure is built in the jack container, and the jack is based on Pascal's law that the pressure of a liquid in a container is the same at all points. When the handle is pressed down, valve A is closed whereas valve B is opened; the hydraulic fluid is forced into the large cylinder and hence pushes the piston moving upward. Because one cylinder has a larger area, the force the larger cylinder produces will be higher, although the pressure in the two cylinders will remain the same. (The car braking system works on the same law: a small force from the driver's foot produces a greater force which acts equally on all four brake pads.)"
                  }
                ]
              }
