                    "q": "3. Explain the construction and working of a Spectroscope.",
                    "a": "The construction and working of a Spectroscope is as follows: (1) Opaque Barrier with a Slit: it forms a narrow beam of light. (2) Prism: it splits the narrow beam of light into its seven component colours. (3) Detector or a Screen: it allows the user to view the resulting spectrum of light. A spectroscope is attached with a telescope to create a spectrum of light coming from a star. It is used in identifying chemical elements in a stellar atmosphere such as carbon, nitrogen, oxygen, etc. Thus, a spectroscope can tell us what elements are present in a star.",
